    "title": "Beaumont United homecoming parade to close roads Wednesday - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Megan Zapalac ,\n1 days ago Beaumont United's band is shown during a high school football game this season. (Kim Brent) A high school homecoming parade is set to cause road closures Wednesday in Beaumont.\nThe Beaumont United High School parade will take place from 5 to 7:30 p.m., causing multiple road closures.\nRELATED: Longtime Beaumont ISD trustee Woodrow Reece II dead at 72\nFannett Road from Sarah Street to South 4th Street will be closed, as well as South 4th Street from Fannett Road to Sarah Street, according to Beaumont police Sgt. Bobby Anderson.\nAfter the parade, there will be a pep rally with a DJ, food trucks, vendor tables, and multiple performances from Beaumont ISD schools.\nSign up for Beaumont Enterprise newsletters here\nRead the original article on beaumontenterprise.com\n7",
